     1,
     "<pre><span>The reactivity sample creates two id=caption; something like<br><br>    output$captionOut &lt;- reactiveText(function() {<br>      input$caption<br>    })<br><br>and <br>    h3(textOutput(&quot;captionOut&quot;))<br><br>would be better. However, the latter produces illegal code (as all h3)<br><br></span><span>    &lt;<span>h3</span>&gt;</span><span>\n<span style=\"background-color:#ddddff\"><span><span></span>      </span><span>&lt;<span>div</span> <span>id</span>=&quot;<a rel=\"nofollow\">captionOut</a>&quot; <span>class</span>=&quot;<a rel=\"nofollow\">shiny-text-output</a>&quot;&gt;</span><span></span><span>&lt;/<span>div</span>&gt;</span><span></span></span></span><span>\n<span></span>    </span><span>&lt;/<span>h3</span>&gt;</span><span></span><br><br>which is &quot;Element div not allowed as child of element h3 in this case&quot;.<br><br></pre>"
    ]
   ]
